      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be useful to print a warning on any mismatch, since it means one of the ports will be running slower than it wants.\n\nAlso, does this do the wrong thing on a sysjump if RO configures a port for 100kbps and then RW configures it for 400kbps?\n\nCould just do:\n\nint controller_kbps[MAX_CONTROLLERS] \u003d {0};\n\nkbps \u003d i2c_ports[i].kbps;\nif (controller_kbps[controller] \u0026\u0026 controller_kbps[controller] !\u003d kbps) {\n  CPRINTS(\"i2c_init(): controller %d speed conflict: %d !\u003d %d\",\n                  controller, kbps, controller_kbps[controller]);\n  kbps \u003d MIN(kbps, controller_kbps[controller]);\n}\ncontroller_kbps[controller] \u003d kbps;",
